<osis xmlns="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.bibletechnologies.net/2003/OSIS/namespace http://www.bibletechnologies.net/osisCore.2.1.1.xsd">
  <osisText osisIDWork="Ebr530_LUK_Hebrew_Consonantal" osisRefWork="bible" xml:lang="he">
    <header>
      <work osisWork="Ebr530_LUK_Hebrew_Consonantal">
        <title>Luke (Vatican, Vat. ebr. 530)</title>
        <date event="original" type="Gregorian">undated</date>
        <description>Hebrew transcription and English translation of Luke from Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Vat. ebr. 530, part 1, fragment 11, folios 1r–2v, transcribed, translated and annotated by Nehemia Gordon.</description>
        <description type="x-contents">Part 1, fragment 11 of a composite volume of fragments. Folios 1r–2v carry Luke 1:1–35 and John 1:1–13 in Hebrew, each with a heading and a chapter heading.</description>
        <description type="x-script">Fully pointed Hebrew. The pointing is irregular by Tiberian standards: dagesh is often omitted where expected, and kamatz and patach — like tsere and segol — are used interchangeably, which the editor relates to the Sephardic pronunciation and to Palestinian pointing (Nikud Eretz-Yisraeli).</description>
        <description type="x-provenance">Held by the Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana and published through its digitisation programme on DigiVatLib.</description>
        <description type="x-editorial">The editor notes that a scribe scratched out Adonai and wrote Yehovah in its place, and records variant forms attested in Mishnaic manuscripts and in the Bar Ilan Responsa Database.</description>
        <publisher>Nehemia Gordon</publisher>
        <type type="x-manuscript">Manuscript</type>
        <identifier type="OSIS">Ebr530_LUK_Hebrew_Consonantal</identifier>
        <identifier type="x-shelfmark">Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Vat. ebr. 530, part 1, fragment 11, folios 1r–2v</identifier>
        <identifier type="URI">https://digi.vatlib.it/view/MSS_Vat.ebr.530.pt.1</identifier>
        <source>Shelfmark, extent and repository from the manuscript's record in DigiVatLib, https://digi.vatlib.it/view/MSS_Vat.ebr.530.pt.1. Codicological detail is catalogued by Umberto Cassuto, 'Codices Vaticani Hebraici' — cited here, not consulted.</source>
        <source>Text, translation and annotation from Nehemia Gordon, 'Hebrew Gospels of Luke and John found in the Vatican Library', version 3.9 (2018), nehemiaswall.com.</source>
        <language>he</language>
        <coverage>Luke 1:1–35</coverage>
        <scope>LUK</scope>
